            <ArticleTitle>Imaging of osteonecrosis of the femoral head.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6-12</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Osteonecrosis of the femoral head is a common disease affecting both children and adults causing acute hip pain and functional impairment. Among the various techniques allowing a correct diagnosis, MRI represents the gold standard for an early detection, the latter being useful for a positive outcome. The purpose of this review is to describe the imaging findings of the osteonecrosis of the femoral head.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
